From: DashBerry <zero/README.md>
Subject: [PATCH] configfs: select H.264 when the format name starts with 'h'

uvc-gadget picks the V4L2 capture fourcc from the FIRST CHARACTER of the
configfs format instance name: 'm' -> MJPEG, 'u' -> YUYV, and nothing else.
That is the entire format-selection logic, which is why a gadget configured
with a framebased/h format would otherwise fall through to 0 and stream
nothing recognisable.

DashBerry needs the Zero to encode H.264 in hardware, because the Pi 4 that
consumes this stream cannot software-encode any usable mode at 30 fps (one
openh264 slice = one thread = ~65,000 macroblocks/s; 720p30 alone wants
108,000). See DashBerry/INVESTIGATE-REAR-ENCODE.md.

The second hunk is diagnostics only: v4l2_get_available_formats() just prints
what the capture device offers, and without H264 in its filter the startup log
stays silent about exactly the formats someone bringing this up is looking for.

Applies to peterbay/uvc-gadget @ e9a733fe5c4a7fcb48e963e8d994bc33d24d814e,
the SHA package/piwebcam/piwebcam.mk pins.
---
diff --git a/uvc-gadget.c b/uvc-gadget.c
index c402125..f147304 100644
--- a/uvc-gadget.c
+++ b/uvc-gadget.c
@@ -1015,7 +1015,9 @@ static void v4l2_get_available_formats()
     fmtdesc.type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE;
 
     while (ioctl(v4l2_dev.fd, VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT, &fmtdesc) == 0) {
-        if (fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MJPEG || fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV) {
+        if (fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MJPEG ||
+            fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV ||
+            fmtdesc.pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264) {
             frmsize.pixel_format = fmtdesc.pixelformat;
             frmsize.index = 0;
             while (ioctl(v4l2_dev.fd, VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES, &frmsize) >= 0) {
@@ -2098,6 +2100,9 @@ static int configfs_video_format(const char * format)
     } else if (!strncmp(format, "u", 1)) {
         return V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV;
 
+    } else if (!strncmp(format, "h", 1)) {
+        return V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264;
+
     }
     return 0;
 }
